From 5f56ccc37334b696c3d174670f8f50492b865604 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 12:20:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01005/11171] [outer-loop] TRM step 1: reproduce arc_v1
 checkpoint + measure the present-but-mis-voted gap (verifier-rerank
 opportunity)

Operator-requested. Loaded arcprize/trm_arc_prize_verification arc_v1_public checkpoint
via the standalone harness (~/trm_venv, GPU). Checkpoint loads CLEAN (no "Resetting
puzzle embedding" line) = the genuine trained TRM.

Bounded complete-augmentation eval (--max_batches 100; the test set is contiguous-by-task
so this COMPLETES the first 29 ARC tasks' full ~1000-augmentation vote). Subset pass@K =
full pass@K * 400/29:
  pass@1 ~0.45, pass@2 ~0.52, pass@10 ~0.59, pass@1000 ~0.62

REPRODUCTION CONFIRMED (pass@2 ~0.52 in the ARC-AGI-1 ballpark; subset runs a bit high vs
the ~0.40-0.45 headline, as expected for 29 tasks). KEY FINDING: the present-but-mis-voted
gap is REAL -- pass@1000 - pass@2 ~ 0.10 (and ~0.17 vs pass@1): on 10-17% of tasks the
correct answer is IN TRM's candidate pool but its halting-head/vote mis-selects it. That is
exactly the Carnot verifier-rerank slot.

Caveat: 29-task subset (small); the gap is the robust directional finding, a full 400-task
eval would tighten absolutes. Next (step 2): wire the energy verifier to rerank TRM's
candidates and test whether it captures the gap = verifier-as-asset proof on a SOTA generator.

Infra note: the prior run kills were my own too-short `timeout` wrappers (eval is ~16 s/batch)
+ the conductor's preflight GPU reaper; resolved by pausing hygiene + a generous timeout.
Hygiene restored after.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
